sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: New-order application inside the gateway
    accDescr: After admission, the gateway consumes the command sequence, checks the order ID, reserves risk, and preflights matching. Business rejection consumes sequence but leaves no new resting order. The event engine publishes the result afterward.
    participant Events as Event engine
    participant GW as Gateway
    participant Risk as Risk
    participant Book as Book

    Note over Events,Book: Sequence and event capacity already admitted
    Events->>GW: Apply NewOrder
    GW->>GW: Recheck and consume sequence
    alt Duplicate or older order ID
        GW-->>Events: Business rejection
    else New order ID
        GW->>GW: Advance order ID watermark
        GW->>Risk: Check and reserve
        alt Risk rejection
            Risk-->>GW: RejectReason
            GW-->>Events: Business rejection
        else Reservation active
            GW->>Book: Build bounded MatchPlan
            Note over Book: Preflight policy,<br/>liquidity and capacity
            alt Book rejection
                Book-->>GW: RejectReason
                GW->>Risk: Release taker reservation
                GW-->>Events: Business rejection
            else Plan accepted
                Book->>Book: Apply fills and<br/>resting remainder
                Book-->>GW: Summary and fixed reports
                loop Each trade report
                    GW->>Risk: Record maker and taker fills
                end
                opt Untraded remainder does not rest
                    GW->>Risk: Release unused taker reservation
                end
                GW-->>Events: NewOrder outcome
            end
        end
    end
    Events->>Events: Publish EventBatch
    Note over Events,Book: Business rejections publish Rejected and consume sequence
    Note over Events,Book: Internal risk or publication failures are fatal
